KPUL0 9.0.0
# A hand-written fixture, NOT generated: it declares a reader this build cannot be, and its
# job is to FAIL to load. If a future change makes it load, the min_consumer gate has
# stopped working -- the failure that let kernels/bin/*.kpubin rot, and the reason R4 exists.
#
# Note the magic is the FIRST line, with comments after it: a file has to be identifiable by
# its opening bytes, so nothing may precede the magic. The first draft of this fixture put
# the comment first and the corpus test caught it -- reporting NotAnL0File where the point
# was to exercise UnsupportedVersion.
MIN_CONSUMER 9.0.0
OPSET tile 9.0.0
PRODUCER hand-written 1.0.0
PROGRAM "from the future"
VALUES none
OPERAND "A" rows=16 cols=16 tile_rows=16 tile_cols=16
OP kind=FEED in=A:0,0 port_kind=input port="West"
END
